          </div>
          <div class="spinefold"></div>
          <div class="spinetext"><span>caithrin · annual 2026</span></div>
          <div class="pageblock"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="spread">
          <div class="pg left">
            <div class="run"><span>caithrin</span><span>Contents</span></div>
            <div class="toc-line"><span class="t">Fearmongering the Frontier</span><span class="dots"></span><span class="n">9</span></div>
            <div class="toc-line"><span class="t">"Helpful Assistant", AI's Original Sin</span><span class="dots"></span><span class="n">21</span></div>
            <div class="toc-line"><span class="t">China Writing &amp; Wall Dancing</span><span class="dots"></span><span class="n">31</span></div>
            <div class="toc-line"><span class="t">so now we all love open models. now what?</span><span class="dots"></span><span class="n">38</span></div>
            <div class="toc-line"><span class="t">First Steps: Pacific Compute</span><span class="dots"></span><span class="n">57</span></div>
            <div class="toc-line"><span class="t">Card Counters of the Soul</span><span class="dots"></span><span class="n">64</span></div>
            <div class="fol">· iv ·</div>
          </div>
          <div class="pg right">
            <div class="run"><span>Annual 2026</span><span>9</span></div>
            <h4>Fearmongering the Frontier</h4>
            <div class="by">August 18 · 2,596 words</div>
            <p class="dc">Typeset from the essay's opening pages: your prose, set at 10.5 on 15
            with article notes, running headers and a folio, exactly as it prints.</p>
            <p>Every article opens on its own page with title, date and byline.</p>
            <div class="fol">· 9 ·</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Typeset render of the design system, not a photograph.</p>
      <table class="spec">
        <tr><td>Trim</td><td>6 × 9 in, perfect bound</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Paper</td><td>60# uncoated white, black ink</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cover</td><td>Full colour, matte, your publication's own masthead and palette</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Length</td><td>30–300 pages; a year of weekly essays is roughly 200</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Apparatus</td><td>Contents with page numbers, running headers, article notes and bylines per article</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Price</td><td>Beta pricing is at cost: readers pay exactly what printing and shipping
        cost, and we add nothing. Measured on a real order: a 294-page collected edition landed for
        $16.58 including tax, mainland US</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Live example</td><td>The first edition is on sale now, at its exact $9.34 print cost:
        <a href="https://www.lulu.com/shop/caithrin-rintoul/caithrin-collected-essays-20252026/paperback/product-m2v2e82.html">caithrin
        &mdash; Collected Essays 2025&ndash;2026</a>. You pay the printer directly; neither we nor the
        author receive a cent on it.</td></tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="kicker">How it works</div>
      <ol class="how">
        <li>Paste your publication's URL above. Free posts come from your public archive; for
        paywalled posts you upload Substack's own export, so no passwords change hands.</li>
        <li>We typeset the issue and send you a proof PDF. You reorder, cut, add an editor's note,
        then lock it.</li>
        <li>Your readers order from one link to a private Lulu listing. Lulu prints each copy on
        demand and mails it to the reader; Inksheaf does not handle their payment.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="kicker">Who the beta is for</div>
      <p>Substack writers with roughly 1,000 to 20,000 subscribers, at least a year of archive, and
      essays or serialized nonfiction. Every publication in the beta gets concierge treatment: a
      person, not a pipeline, checks every page of your first issue.</p>
      <p>Three ways beta publications plan to use print: a founding-member perk, with sponsored
      copies for top supporters under a budget cap you set; an annual readers buy from a link in
      your footer or About page; and a door into the back catalog, so a new subscriber can meet
      three years of writing as one bound volume instead of an infinite scroll.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="kicker">Questions writers ask</div>
      <dl class="faq">
        <dt>What does it cost me?</dt>
        <dd>Nothing during the beta. Readers pay printing and shipping at cost, with nothing added:
        a 294-page book landed at $16.58 on a real order, and thinner books cost less.</dd>
        <dt>What do I earn?</dt>
        <dd>During the beta, nothing and neither do we: books sell at cost. The author revenue share
        gets designed with beta publications afterward, on measured numbers.</dd>
        <dt>Who owns the writing?</dt>
        <dd>You do. You grant permission to print and mail the copies your readers order, and you
        can revoke it at any time; revoking stops sales of your editions.</dd>
        <dt>How do paid posts get in without my password?</dt>
        <dd>You upload the export Substack generates in your own dashboard (Settings → Exports).
        Any subscriber files inside it are discarded unread; only the posts are kept.</dd>
        <dt>What happens to images, tweets and embeds?</dt>
        <dd>Missing images are flagged automatically and the print proof is checked by a person.
        Web-only embeds are omitted or replaced with a printed source note. You see the result
        before the issue is locked.</dd>
        <dt>When do the first books exist?</dt>
        <dd>The beta targets December printing, with books in readers' hands around New Year. Beta
        publications hear every date change directly.</dd>
        <dt>Where can I read more?</dt>
        <dd>Write to <a href="mailto:hello@inksheaf.com">hello@inksheaf.com</a>; every message gets
        an answer. The build is documented as it happens on
        <a href="https://www.caithrin.com">caithrin.com</a>.</dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="beta" id="beta">
      <div class="kicker">Join the private beta</div>
      <div class="steps">Step <b id="stepnum">1</b> of 2</div>
      <form id="f" novalidate>
        <input class="hp" type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />

        <div class="step1">
          <label for="url">Your publication's URL</label>
          <input type="url" id="url" name="publication_url" placeholder="https://yourname.substack.com" required />
          <button type="button" class="main" data-next="2">Continue</button>
        </div>

        <div class="step2">
          <div class="prefilled" id="carried"></div>
          <label for="email">Where should we send the first proof pages?</label>
          <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required />
          <input type="hidden" name="posts_per_year" id="ppy" />
          <input type="hidden" name="frequency" />
          <button type="submit" class="main">Request a spot</button>
          <button type="button" class="ghost" data-back="1">Back</button>
        </div>

        <div class="err" id="err" role="alert"></div>
      </form>
      <div class="done" id="done">
        <h3>You're on the list.</h3>
        <p>We reply to every signup within a few days with the beta timeline and, if your archive is
        public, the first proof pages of your own edition. To skip the queue, reply with a link to
        the one issue of your publication you'd most want on paper.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <img class="mark mark-l" src="/brand/mark-black-sm.png" alt="" height="34" /><img class="mark mark-d" src="/brand/mark-white-sm.png" alt="" height="34" />
    Inksheaf prints editions of Substack publications with their owners' permission. It is an
    independent product, for Substack writers, and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Substack Inc.<br />
    US delivery during the beta. Built by <a href="https://about.caithrin.com">Caithrin</a>.
    · <a href="mailto:hello@inksheaf.com">hello@inksheaf.com</a>
  </footer>
</div>

<script>
const f = document.getElementById('f') as HTMLFormElement;
const sid = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2,10);
const seen = new Set();
function beacon(ev: string){
  if (seen.has(ev)) return; seen.add(ev);
  navigator.sendBeacon?.('/api/event', new Blob(
    [JSON.stringify({session:sid, event:ev})], {type:'application/json'}));
}
beacon('view');
function show(n: number){
  for (const k of [1,2]) (f.querySelector('.step'+k) as HTMLElement).style.display = (k===n?'block':'none');
  document.getElementById('stepnum')!.textContent = String(n);
  document.getElementById('err')!.textContent = '';
  if (n>1) beacon('step'+n);
}
show(1);

/* ---------- live preview ---------- */
const trybtn = document.getElementById('trybtn') as HTMLButtonElement;
const tryurl = document.getElementById('tryurl') as HTMLInputElement;
const tryerr = document.getElementById('tryerr')!;
let previewData: any = null;

/* ---------- typesetting interlude: facts fade through while the press runs ---------- */
const stage = document.getElementById('pv-stage')!;
const setline = document.getElementById('pv-setline')!;
let lastShownHost: string | null = null;
const motionOK = !matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
async function beat(html: string, hold = 620){
  setline.classList.remove('in'); setline.classList.add('out');
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 230));
  setline.innerHTML = html;
  setline.classList.remove('out'); setline.classList.add('in');
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 290 + hold));
}
function interludeStart(){
  if (!motionOK) return false;
  const pv = document.getElementById('preview')!;
  pv.classList.remove('on'); pv.classList.add('staging');
  setline.innerHTML = 'Reading your archive&hellip;';
  setline.classList.add('in');
  stage.classList.add('on');
  stage.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'center'});
  return true;
}
async function interludeFacts(d: any){
  const mon = (iso: string) => new Date(iso + 'T00:00:00Z')
    .toLocaleDateString('en-US', {month:'long', year:'numeric', timeZone:'UTC'});
  await beat('<b>' + d.posts + '</b> ' + (d.posts === 1 ? 'essay.' : 'essays.'));
  await beat('<b>' + d.words.toLocaleString('en-US') + '</b> words.');
  await beat(mon(d.from) + ' &ndash; ' + mon(d.to) + '.');
  await beat('That makes a <b>' + d.est_pages + '-page</b> book.', 780);
  stage.classList.remove('on');
  setline.classList.remove('in');
  document.getElementById('preview')!.classList.remove('staging');
}

async function runPreview(attempt = 0, originalRaw: string | null = null){
  const raw = originalRaw ?? tryurl.value.trim();
  if (!raw){ tryerr.textContent = 'Paste your publication URL first.'; return; }
  tryerr.textContent = '';
  trybtn.disabled = true; trybtn.textContent = 'Typesetting…';
  const interludeOn = attempt === 0 && tryurl.value && raw !== lastShownHost ? interludeStart() : false;
  try {
    const r = await fetch('/api/preview?url=' + encodeURIComponent(raw));
    const d = await r.json();
    if (!d.ok){
      if (d.error === 'upstream_busy' && attempt === 0){
        for (let t = 4; t > 0; t--){
          if (tryurl.value.trim() !== raw) return;
          tryerr.textContent = 'Substack is rate-limiting us for a moment. Retrying in ' + t + 's…';
          await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, 1000));
        }
        tryerr.textContent = '';
        return runPreview(1, raw);
      }
      (f.elements.namedItem('publication_url') as HTMLInputElement).value =
        raw.startsWith('http') ? raw : 'https://' + raw;
      stage.classList.remove('on');
      document.getElementById('preview')!.classList.remove('staging');
      tryerr.textContent = d.message || 'Could not read that archive.'; return;
    }
    previewData = d;
    if (interludeOn && d.host !== lastShownHost) await interludeFacts(d);
    else { stage.classList.remove('on'); document.getElementById('preview')!.classList.remove('staging'); }
    lastShownHost = d.host;
    renderPreview(d);
    history.replaceState(null, '', '?pub=' + encodeURIComponent(d.host));
  } catch {
    stage.classList.remove('on');
    document.getElementById('preview')!.classList.remove('staging');
    tryerr.textContent = 'Could not reach the preview service. The signup below works without it.';
  } finally {
    trybtn.disabled = false; trybtn.textContent = 'Show my book';
  }
}
function renderPreview(d: any){
  const months = Math.max(1, Math.round((Date.parse(d.to) - Date.parse(d.from)) / 2629800000));
  const kind = (months > 7 && d.est_pages <= 300) ? 'Annual' : 'Quarterly';
  (document.getElementById('pv-kind') as HTMLElement).textContent = kind + ' · ' + d.to.slice(0,4);
  (document.getElementById('pv-mast') as HTMLElement).textContent = d.publication;
  (document.getElementById('pv-dates') as HTMLElement).textContent = fmt(d.from) + ' – ' + fmt(d.to);
  (document.getElementById('pv-cvpages') as HTMLElement).textContent = d.est_pages > 300
    ? 'Vol. I of IV · est. ' + Math.round(d.est_pages/4) + ' pages'
    : d.posts + (d.capped ? '+' : '') + ' posts · est. ' + d.est_pages + ' pages';
  (document.getElementById('pv-spine') as HTMLElement).textContent = d.publication + ' · ' + d.to.slice(0,4);
  const over = d.est_pages > 300;

  /* their colors on their cover (contrast-guarded server-side) */
  const book = document.getElementById('pvbook') as HTMLElement;
  if (d.theme){
    book.classList.add('branded');
    book.style.setProperty('--pvbg', d.theme.cover_bg);
    book.style.setProperty('--pvink', d.theme.cover_ink);
    book.style.setProperty('--pvink2', d.theme.cover_ink2);
    if (d.theme.heading_stack) book.style.setProperty('--pvfont', d.theme.heading_stack);
  } else {
    book.classList.remove('branded');
  }

  /* their titles become the contents page */
  const toc = document.getElementById('pv-toc')!;
  (document.getElementById('pv-runname') as HTMLElement).textContent = d.publication;
  const rows = (d.sample && d.sample.length ? d.sample.map((x: any) => x.t) : (d.titles || [])).slice(0, 6);
  const step = Math.max(3, Math.round(d.est_pages / Math.max(d.posts, 1)));
  let folio = 9;
  toc.innerHTML = rows.map((t: string, i: number) => {
    const line = '<div class="toc-line" style="transition-delay:' + (0.45 + i * 0.12) + 's">' +
      '<span class="t"></span><span class="dots"></span><span class="n">' + folio + '</span></div>';
    folio += step;
    return line;
  }).join('');
  [...toc.querySelectorAll('.t')].forEach((el, i) => (el as HTMLElement).textContent = rows[i]);

  /* print estimate from the measured production-cost curve; shipping and tax stay separate */
  const pricePages = over ? Math.round(d.est_pages / 4) : d.est_pages;
  const dollars = Math.round(2 + 0.025 * pricePages);
  (document.getElementById('pv-price') as HTMLElement).innerHTML =
    'Estimated printing: <b>about $' + dollars + (over ? ' a volume' : '') + '</b>' +
    '<span class="sub">Shipping and tax are calculated by Lulu. Inksheaf adds nothing during the beta.</span>';

  /* staged assembly: cover lands, then the spine thickens to their page count */
  const block = document.getElementById('pv-block') as HTMLElement;
  block.style.width = '5px';
  requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    block.style.width = Math.max(5, Math.min(14, Math.round(d.est_pages / 22))) + 'px';
  }));
  (document.getElementById('pv-big') as HTMLElement).innerHTML = over
    ? 'Your year is a <b>' + d.est_pages.toLocaleString('en-US') + '-page shelf</b>.'
    : 'Your archive is already a <b>' + d.est_pages + '-page book</b>.';
  (document.getElementById('pv-sub') as HTMLElement).textContent =
    d.posts + (d.capped ? '+' : '') + ' public posts, ' + d.words.toLocaleString('en-US') +
    ' words, ' + fmt(d.from) + ' to ' + fmt(d.to) + '. ' + (over
    ? 'Too big for one binding, so it prints as quarterly volumes of about ' + Math.round(d.est_pages/4) + ' pages each.'
    : 'Typeset at 6×9 with contents, running headers and your own cover.');
  const pv = document.getElementById('preview')!;
  pv.classList.remove('on');
  void (pv as HTMLElement).offsetWidth;
  pv.classList.add('on');
  pv.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth', block:'center'});
}
function fmt(iso: string){
  return new Date(iso + 'T00:00:00Z').toLocaleDateString('en-US', {month:'short', year:'numeric', timeZone:'UTC'});
}
trybtn.addEventListener('click', ()=>runPreview());
tryurl.addEventListener('keydown', (e)=>{ if (e.key==='Enter'){ e.preventDefault(); runPreview(); } });
{ /* a preview someone shares reproduces itself */
  const pub = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('pub');
  if (pub && /^[a-z0-9.-]+$/i.test(pub)){ tryurl.value = 'https://' + pub; runPreview(); }
}

(document.getElementById('pv-cta') as HTMLButtonElement).addEventListener('click', ()=>{
  const d = previewData;
  if (d){
    (f.elements.namedItem('publication_url') as HTMLInputElement).value = 'https://' + d.host;
    (f.elements.namedItem('posts_per_year') as HTMLInputElement).value = String(d.posts);
    (f.elements.namedItem('frequency') as HTMLInputElement).value =
      d.posts >= 200 ? 'daily' : d.posts >= 40 ? 'weekly' : d.posts >= 10 ? 'monthly' : 'irregular';
    document.getElementById('carried')!.textContent =
      d.publication + ' · ' + d.est_pages + ' estimated pages. Leave one email for the first proof pages.';
    show(2);
  }
  document.getElementById('beta')!.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'});
});

/* ---------- funnel ---------- */
f.addEventListener('keydown', (e)=>{
  if (e.key !== 'Enter') return;
  const target = e.target as HTMLElement;
  if (target.tagName === 'BUTTON' || target.tagName === 'SELECT') return;
  const current = [1,2].find(k => (f.querySelector('.step'+k) as HTMLElement).style.display !== 'none');
  if (current && current < 2){
    e.preventDefault();
    (f.querySelector('.step'+current+' [data-next]') as HTMLElement)?.click();
  }
});
f.addEventListener('click', (e)=>{
  const t = e.target as HTMLElement;
  const next = t.dataset?.next, back = t.dataset?.back;
  if (back) return show(+back);
  if (!next) return;
  if (next==='2'){
    const u = (f.elements.namedItem('publication_url') as HTMLInputElement).value.trim();
    try { new URL(u.startsWith('http')?u:'https://'+u); } catch {
      document.getElementById('err')!.textContent = 'That does not look like a URL.';
      return;
    }
    if (!u.startsWith('http')) (f.elements.namedItem('publication_url') as HTMLInputElement).value = 'https://'+u;
  }
  show(+next);
});
f.addEventListener('submit', async (e)=>{
  e.preventDefault();
  const email = (f.elements.namedItem('email') as HTMLInputElement).value.trim();
  if (!/^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$/.test(email)){
    document.getElementById('err')!.textContent = 'That email does not look right.';
    return;
  }
  const data = Object.fromEntries(new FormData(f).entries());
  const r = await fetch('/api/signup', {method:'POST',
    headers:{'content-type':'application/json'}, body: JSON.stringify(data)});
  if (r.ok){
    beacon('signup');
    (f as HTMLElement).style.display='none';
    (document.querySelector('.steps') as HTMLElement).style.display='none';
    document.getElementById('done')!.style.display='block';
  } else {
    document.getElementById('err')!.textContent = 'Something failed on our side. Email hello@inksheaf.com and we will add you by hand.';
  }
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
